\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Stage 3: the five continual-learning methods}, top to bottom from the input clips to the loss. All train the same network (blue) with a head that grows by the new classes; they differ only in what protects the old classes: nothing (S3.0), a weight penalty $\Omega =\genfrac  {}{}{}1{\lambda }{2}\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _i F_i(\theta _i-\theta _i^\star )^2$ (S3.1), the scores of a frozen copy of the old model (S3.2, dashed), stored old clips (S3.3, orange), or both (S3.4). Bottom: final accuracy on all 20 classes (Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:cl}).}}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cl}{{3}{5}{\textbf {Stage 3: the five continual-learning methods}, top to bottom from the input clips to the loss. All train the same network (blue) with a head that grows by the new classes; they differ only in what protects the old classes: nothing (S3.0), a weight penalty $\Omega =\tfrac {\lambda }{2}\sum _i F_i(\theta _i-\theta _i^\star )^2$ (S3.1), the scores of a frozen copy of the old model (S3.2, dashed), stored old clips (S3.3, orange), or both (S3.4). Bottom: final accuracy on all 20 classes (Table~\ref {tab:cl})}{figure.3}{}}
