\citation{radford2021clip}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Stage 4: the five distillation objectives}, top to bottom. The pretrained student (blue, left of each panel) always learns from the labels (CE); the frozen teacher (dashed, right) adds nothing (S4.0), its softened scores (S4.1), its clip feature by direction (S4.2), its clip feature through a learnable regressor $g$ (S4.3), or KD plus the nearest of 3 KMeans prototypes of the student's class (S4.4, new; detail in Fig.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:proto}). Bottom: student test accuracy (\%) with the full training set $|$ with 32 clips per class (Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:kd}).}}{7}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:kd}{{4}{7}{\textbf {Stage 4: the five distillation objectives}, top to bottom. The pretrained student (blue, left of each panel) always learns from the labels (CE); the frozen teacher (dashed, right) adds nothing (S4.0), its softened scores (S4.1), its clip feature by direction (S4.2), its clip feature through a learnable regressor $g$ (S4.3), or KD plus the nearest of 3 KMeans prototypes of the student's class (S4.4, new; detail in Fig.~\ref {fig:proto}). Bottom: student test accuracy (\%) with the full training set $|$ with 32 clips per class (Table~\ref {tab:kd})}{figure.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {S4.4 Proto-align in detail.} (1) Once, before training, the frozen teacher encodes the training clips of every class and KMeans groups their 256-d features into 3 prototypes per class (stars). (2) At every step the student learns from the label (CE), from the teacher's softened scores (KD), and from a prototype term that pulls its clip feature $h_s$ to the nearest prototype of its own class $y$, $\qopname  \relax m{min}_j\lVert h_s-\mu _{y,j}\rVert ^2$. The teacher and the prototypes are never updated; only the student (blue) trains.}}{7}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:proto}{{5}{7}{\textbf {S4.4 Proto-align in detail.} (1) Once, before training, the frozen teacher encodes the training clips of every class and KMeans groups their 256-d features into 3 prototypes per class (stars). (2) At every step the student learns from the label (CE), from the teacher's softened scores (KD), and from a prototype term that pulls its clip feature $h_s$ to the nearest prototype of its own class $y$, $\min _j\lVert h_s-\mu _{y,j}\rVert ^2$. The teacher and the prototypes are never updated; only the student (blue) trains}{figure.5}{}}
